maria: quick note 1: i'm about to open a tiny PR to simplify the 429/error-ref entry. it currently duplicates backoff examples and points at an outdated SDK anchor. i'll replace with a single clear JS + py snippet, add a short Retry-After parsing helper, and update the cross-links. will push in ~15m.
ashwin: love it. please include an exact hosted SDK call (copy-pasteable) and the recommended retry config: maxRetries, capped exponential base, cap, jitter. folks keep copying non-terminating loops.
kevin: also add a short helper to parse Retry-After that handles both numeric seconds and http-date (RFC1123). a one-liner or tiny function is fine.
maria: thinking of this minimal JS example + helper:
```js
// prefer Retry-After header, else capped exp backoff with jitter
function parseRetryAfter(header) {
  if (!header) return null;
  const secs = Number(header);
  if (!isNaN(secs)) return secs * 1000;
  const date = Date.parse(header);
  return isNaN(date) ? null : Math.max(0, date - Date.now());
}
const res = await redwood.generate({ model: 'redwood-xsmall', input: prompt });
if (res.status === 429) {
  const wait = parseRetryAfter(res.headers['retry-after']) ?? Math.min(5000, 200 * 2 ** attempt + jitter());
  await sleep(wait);
  retry();
}
```
elaine: please add a one-sentence note under "fallback behavior" recommending when to prefer a lower-capacity variant vs using a quantized fallback (hint: prefer a model variant if quality matters; quantized fallback for latency/cost constraints). also update the link-checker job1: CI flagged the old anchor earlier.
